WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always great to see you.
We met in this building.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we did.
-In 2001.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have had a --
Your acting career has thrived

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.007 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Mine came to a dead end.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we did --
We did act together

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:12.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
in one of the finest sketche
that ever aired on "SNL."

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The "Fenced-In Area."
-"Fenced-In Area."

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.550
We actually talked about
this sketch just last week

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the writer of it,
Emily Spivey, who was here

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.822
And this a sketch -- You playe
a simple man in this sketch.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. Yes.
-You just had a fenced-in area

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were trying
to figure out what do with it.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.595 line:92%
-That's all I wanted to know

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.463 line:92%
I just -- I had the space.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.364 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I had the chain link.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wanted to do
something important with it.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you still get --
People still come up to yo

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.807
about "Fenced-In Area."
-It's the weirdest thing.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will confirm
that's a weird thing, yeah

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.913 size:84% position:42%
-Right? And that's like
nearly 20 years ago.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one skit
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And people still, you know --

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:55.488
Somebody will come up to me,
and I'll go, "Okay, here we go."

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to be, you know
"I loved 'Armageddon.'"

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I love 'Sling Blade.'"
I love whatever.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.296 line:92%
"Oh, my God. 'Monster's Ball.'

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they come up, and they go,
"Dude, 'Fenced-In Area'?"

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a great show.
"Goliath" is a great show.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.209 line:92%
Third season. You take --

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:19.479
You play an alcoholic lawyer who
takes on wealthy corporations.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the great things
about it --

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.983 line:92%
Wonderful foils against you.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
William Hurt.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.387 line:92%
Dennis Quaid this season.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.788 line:92%
Mark Duplass. Morris Chestnut.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:29.856 line:92%
Do you enjoy this character?

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems like
it's a pretty meaty part.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love it. I mean, it's
probably closer to myself --

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:37.330 size:75% position:38%
I mean, not that I'm
an alcoholic lawyer.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But I --

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.369 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No one thinks you're a lawyer
Billy Bob.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.642 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.712 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So, yeah.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, I mean, it's kind of like
I just go to work every da

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
and do what I would do
if I were that guy.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
And after a while,
after you play a character

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a couple of seasons
on something,

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.157 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you start to feel like

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
the stuff's actually happening
to you. You know?

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, you do.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get to work.
You're in this scene.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.263 line:92%
And it's like, "Oh, really?"

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Dennis Quaid, you know
he's my old buddy.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.436
You know, we've been running
buddies for probably 25 years.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was great
having him on there because,

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.876
you know, we -- You get busy
in the entertainment business,

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
and you don't see each other

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
We live like 1/2 mile
from each other.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then we were
working together,

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.582
so I got to see him every day.
And they made the huge mistake

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
of putting our trailers
next to each other.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.254 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And there was a lot of,

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:38.291 size:84% position:42%
"Has anybody seen Billy
or Dennis?" going on.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:38.825 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah. So --

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:41.861 size:81% position:41%
-You have had trouble
with the law, run-ins,

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:45.832 size:88% position:44%
but at a very young age,
growing up in Arkansas,

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
the FBI,
did they raid your house?

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was my grandmother's house
-Okay.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why did the FBI raid
your grandmother's house?

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I was --
See, I was only like 3.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to understand, or 4.
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.279 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I was a little kid.

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:02.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
My uncle, my mom's brother
he was kind of a --

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:05.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was a traveling
country musician kind of guy

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.520 size:75% position:38% line:92%
part-time carpenter.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.788 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:11.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he always had
these weird friends

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.493 line:92%
he would bring home from Texas

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:16.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this guy came home
with him one time

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:18.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, sort of
like a con artist,

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, smooth talker.
-Sure.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.435
-And a bunch of us lived
at my grandmother's house.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were very poor,
so we all lived there --

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, cousins and aunts an
uncles, all in this one house.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:29.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this guy was just ther
with my uncle.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
And suddenly he stayed
for like a month.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And then one day,

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:36.082 line:92%
the FBI just came in there

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and carted him off.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.687 line:92%
And turns out he was really fond

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
of stealing
other people's vehicles

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
and taking them
across state lines.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:47.594
And my grandfather, who wa
kind of like Daniel Boone,

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:50.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
had killed a giant turtle,
and he was making turtle soup.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:53.766
And he was one of those guys -
He was a medic in World War I,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he'd seen everything,
you know?

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.503 size:84% position:42%
And he's standing there
cleaning this turtle

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.371 size:75% position:38% line:92%
to make turtle soup.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:00.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
And an FBI guy
comes to the back door.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.676
And my grandfather said, "Di
you ever see a turtle that big?"

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:07.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That is --

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a guy
who keeps your cool.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Keeps his cool.

